Phase 2 architecture decision
Phase 2 should extend the existing Next.js backend—not introduce another framework—and organize it as:
Route/controller → service → repository interface → memory/postgres implementation
Repository selection will remain environment-driven, for example:
BUYER_PROFILE_REPOSITORY=memory|postgres
DATABASE_URL=...
BANK_VERIFICATION_PROVIDER=mock|production-provider
Passwords and bank-account numbers will not be stored in plaintext. Password changes will go through an authentication-provider interface; bank data will use a tokenized/encrypted provider interface.
